# interplay_fifo_token_ring_wrap: A token passed around four FIFOs for eight rounds while every ring wraps: each exec increments a counter (inc_k) and copies it to log[k], and is gated on the previous FIFO's exec. Each exec command is 0x1554 bytes (its payload padded), so the root's 0x3c00-byte ring and the children's one-page rings wrap more than twice, with commands, headers and barriers straddling their ends. The guest writes two rounds at a time, rings all four doorbells, and waits for the last stamp. The 32 interrupts come in token order, the counter is 32, and log[k] = k + 1: each exec saw every earlier one's write.
